NNAAMMEE
       postdrop - Postfix mail posting utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppoossttddrroopp [--rrvv] [--cc _c_o_n_f_i_g___d_i_r]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ppoossttddrroopp(1)  command  creates a file in the mmaaiillddrroopp directory and
       copies its standard input to the file.

       Options:

       --cc _c_o_n_f_i_g___d_i_r
              The mmaaiinn..ccff configuration file is in the named directory instead
              of the default configuration directory. See also the MAIL_CONFIG
              environment setting below.

       --rr     Use a Postfix-internal protocol for  reading  the  message  from
              standard input, and for reporting status information on standard
              output. This is currently the only supported method.

       --vv     Enable  verbose  logging for debugging purposes. Multiple --vv op‐
              tions make the software increasingly verbose. As of Postfix 2.3,
              this option is available for the super-user only.

SSEECCUURRIITTYY
       The command is designed to run with set-group ID privileges, so that it
       can write to the mmaaiillddrroopp queue directory and so that it can connect to
       Postfix daemon processes.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
       Fatal errors: malformed input, I/O error, out of memory.  Problems  are
       logged  to  ssyyssllooggdd(8) or ppoossttllooggdd(8) and to the standard error stream.
       When the input is incomplete, or when the process receives a HUP,  INT,
       QUIT or TERM signal, the queue file is deleted.

